The native backend

The backend is written in small languages, and this directory is all of it:

  lang/       the languages, each a reader from a file of its own to Coil
  backend/, a64/, x64/, direct/, a64-direct/, x64-direct/, cir/, native/
              the files written in them, made Coil by those readers as the
              compiler compiles
  rt/         the runtime the languages' output stands on, written by hand
  adapter/    from the compiler's CIR to the backend, written by hand (the part
              written once for both machines is adapter/machine.coil)
  tests/      its own tests

Where it comes from

The backend began as coil-stogir (https://github.com/jimmyhmiller/coil-stogir),
a Coil port and adaptation of IR, which it was then rewritten from, language
first, in coil-stogir-declarative
(https://github.com/jimmyhmiller/coil-stogir-declarative). Its graph, the
analyses and passes over it, the split-interval register allocator and its
emission take IR as their reference.

